  "id": "Compound::DB01161 - Gene::6336",
  "verbalization": "Chloroprocaine, through its structural similarity to bromopride and proparacaine, is linked to Scn10a via a shared binding mechanism. The evidence suggests that chloroprocaine, as a member of the anesthetic agent class, binds to Scn10a, which is a key ion channel involved in neuronal signaling. This binding is supported by the lowest common ancestor relationship between chloroprocaine and proparacaine, both of which are classified under the anesthetic agent category and bind to Scn10a. The structural resemblance between chloroprocaine and bromopride further reinforces the notion of a shared pharmacological profile, suggesting that chloroprocaine may exert its effects through a similar mechanism as proparacaine. The integration of these relationships highlights a potential role for chloroprocaine in modulating Scn10a function, possibly through anesthetic action.",
